WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:06.700
Now we know that square root of 2 is an Irrational number.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:10.640
If you use a calculator to calculate the value of Root 2

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:17.320
you will get something like 1.4142135 and so on.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.000
This value that you get is actually non-terminating.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.900
It is never ending.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:27.880
Also, you will not find any pattern in the digits after the decimal.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.340
Hence, it's also called a non-recurring decimal.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.640
There is no pattern that occurs again and again.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:38.600
These kinds of numbers are called Irrational numbers.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.660
Consider square root of 3 for instance.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:48.220
You will get its value as 1.732050 and so on.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.020
Even this decimal is non-terminating and non-recurring.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:57.260
So root 3 is also an Irrational number.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:03.160
You can try calculating the values of root 5, root 6, root 7 or root 8,

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.420
you will find that all of them result

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.860
in non-terminating, non-recurring decimals.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.700
But wait... root 9 equals 3. This is a Rational number.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:18.820
Yes, root 9 is not an Irrational number.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.860
In fact, square root of any perfect square will be a Rational number.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:27.580
But the square root of any number which is not a perfect square

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:31.060
will always result in an Irrational number.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:35.460
Here's the interesting part. If you know these two points well,

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:40.560
you can even form an Irrational number by yourself. Let's see how.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:46.640
We have to form a number which does not end and does not repeat any pattern.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:56.280
Something like 2.01001000100001 and so on.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:02:00.960
Here, the number does not end and is also non-recurring.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:04.340
This means that there is no pattern that repeats forever.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:15.560
You can even have a number like 15.2349449444944449 and so on

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:21.040
This is also Irrational as it is non-terminating and non-recurring.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.820
Where does this concept help us?

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:30.840
Say your are asked to find two Irrational numbers between 1.23 and 1.25.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:35.820
Remember, 1.24 is incorrect as its terminating.

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:39.420
We need a non-terminating, non-recurring decimal.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:40.900
Yes, but we know

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:44.220
that 1.24 is between these two numbers.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:52.240
After 1.24 we can start writing 010010001 and so on.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:55.740
That's one Irrational number between these two numbers.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:59.420
Again, let's write 1.24 and this time

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:05.260
we write 020020002 and so on after it.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.980
That's your second Irrational number.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.220
So to find Irrational numbers between two numbers,

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:14.560
just write a Rational number between them and then add

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:19.020
non-terminating, non-recurring digits after it.

